  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure caused by filesystem permissions on upload directory, not disk or database.\n\n**Root cause: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` not writable by app user**\n\n- App runs as `1000:1000` (E5) and uploads dir is owned `1000:1000` with mode `0555` with `app_user_can_write: false` (E4).\n- Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `0755` with `app_user_can_write: true` (E9), so problem is isolated to `uploads/` subdirectory, not parent.\n- Bind mount `/srv/lab-data -> /data` is `rw: true` (E5), so not a read-only mount - denial is directory mode bits.\n- App logs show direct failure:\n  `os.replace(tmp_path, final_path)` -> `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/...part' -> '/data/uploads/...'` on `POST /upload` returning `500` (E7).\n  Health probe `open(probe,\"wb\")` -> `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-...'` with `health check failed` and `GET /health 503` (E7).\n- Current `/health` is `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2), consistent as symptom of same write failure.\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n- Disk/full inodes: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.6`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E3).\n- Database dependency: `incidentlab-db-1` `running`, `health: healthy` (E6), `Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E8), repeated `pg_isready ... exec_die exit 0` and `health_status: healthy` (E10).\n- App crash/OOM: `incidentlab-app-1 running`, `exit_code: 0`, `oom_killed: false` (E5), both containers `running` (E1).\n\nRecent restarts `Up 4 seconds` / `Up 10 seconds` (E1) with `die exit 0` then `start` for both containers (E10) are operational noise, not cause - DB recovered healthy, app now fails on writes.\n",
